<section class="ac-character-creator ac-shell">
  <header class="ac-wizard-header">
    <div>
      <span class="ac-kicker">GUIDED DHF INITIALISATION</span>
      <h1>Character Creator</h1>
      <p>Build the character in the same order the sheet is organised. Each stage explains what the choice means, where it appears, and what the system calculates for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ac-wizard-counter" data-step-counter>01 / 07</div>
  </header>

  <div class="ac-wizard-progress"><span class="ac-wizard-progress-fill"></span></div>

  <div class="ac-wizard-layout">
    <aside class="ac-wizard-rail" aria-label="Character creation steps">
      {{#each steps}}
      <button type="button" data-action="jumpStep" data-step-index="{{index}}" class="{{#if @first}}active{{/if}}">
        <span>{{number}}</span><div><strong>{{label}}</strong><small>{{#if @first}}Begin here{{else}}Character build{{/if}}</small></div><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i>
      </button>
      {{/each}}
    </aside>

    <main class="ac-wizard-stage">
      <section class="ac-wizard-step active" data-wizard-step="0">
        <div class="ac-step-heading"><span>STEP 01</span><h2>Who is the DHF?</h2><p>Start with the person, not the body. These details persist when the character changes sleeves.</p></div>
        <div class="ac-wizard-grid">
          <article class="ac-panel">
            <header class="ac-panel-title"><span>Persistent Identity</span><small>DHF RECORD</small></header>
            <div class="ac-field-grid one">
              <label><span>True DHF Name <em>The character's actual persistent identity.</em></span><input name="name" value="New DHF" data-live-summary></label>
              <label><span>Public / Current Name <em>The name shown on the Actor and used by people around them. Leave blank to use the true name.</em></span><input name="publicName" value="" data-live-summary></label>
              <label><span>Pronouns <em>Pronouns for the DHF identity; sleeve presentation can be recorded separately.</em></span><input name="pronouns" value="" placeholder="they/them, she/her, he/him…"></label>
              <label><span>DHF Age <em>Total lived age. This feeds the 2020 age-based starting resource and Baggage procedures.</em></span><input type="number" name="age" value="30" min="18" data-live-summary></label>
            </div>
          </article>
          <aside class="ac-explainer">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-id-card"></i>
            <h3>What appears on the sheet?</h3>
            <p><strong>True DHF</strong> is the person who survives resleeving. <strong>Public Name</strong> is the current identity people see. <strong>DHF Age</strong> is not the apparent age of the body; the sleeve tracks that separately.</p>
            <div class="ac-callout">You can change names, pronouns and objectives later without rebuilding the character.</div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ac-wizard-step" data-wizard-step="1">
        <div class="ac-step-heading"><span>STEP 02</span><h2>Choose an Archetype</h2><p>The Archetype is the broad career/life chassis. It establishes the starting Skill profile, Wealth baseline and access/commonality patterns used by the rules.</p></div>
        <div class="ac-wizard-grid">
          <article class="ac-panel">
            <label class="ac-select-field"><span>Archetype</span><select name="archetype" data-live-summary>{{#each archetypes}}<option value="{{name}}" data-default-sleeve="{{defaultSleeve}}">{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
            <label class="ac-select-field"><span>Starting Package</span><select name="package" data-live-summary><option value="">Custom / choose later</option>{{#each packageOptions}}<option value="{{value}}" data-archetype="{{archetype}}">{{label}}</option>{{/each}}</select><small>Starting Packages belong to one Archetype. The wizard filters the list automatically.</small></label>
          </article>
          <aside class="ac-explainer">
            {{#each archetypes}}
            <div data-archetype-panel="{{name}}" {{#unless @first}}hidden{{/unless}}>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-diagram-project"></i><h3>{{name}}</h3>
              <p>Default sleeve suggestion: <strong>{{defaultSleeve}}</strong> · Wealth baseline: <strong>{{wealth}}</strong></p>
              <ul>{{#each features}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{/each}}</ul>
              <div class="ac-callout">Packages: {{#each packages}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}} · {{/unless}}{{/each}}</div>
            </div>
            {{/each}}
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ac-wizard-step" data-wizard-step="2">
        <div class="ac-step-heading"><span>STEP 03</span><h2>Choose a Character Variant</h2><p>Most characters should start as Standard. Advanced variants alter continuity, resources, Virtual behaviour or social rules.</p></div>
        <div class="ac-wizard-grid">
          <article class="ac-panel">
            <label class="ac-select-field"><span>Variant</span><select name="variant" data-live-summary>{{#each variants}}<option value="{{id}}">{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
            <div class="ac-choice-list">
              {{#each variants}}
              <div class="ac-choice-preview"><span>{{tag}}</span><strong>{{name}}</strong><small>{{description}}</small></div>
              {{/each}}
            </div>
          </article>
          <aside class="ac-explainer">
            {{#each variants}}
            <div data-variant-panel="{{id}}" {{#unless @first}}hidden{{/unless}}><i class="fa-solid fa-brain"></i><h3>{{name}}</h3><p>{{description}}</p>{{#if @first}}<div class="ac-callout">Recommended for players learning the system.</div>{{else}}<div class="ac-callout">Advanced rules remain visible in the Rules Browser and on the finished sheet.</div>{{/if}}</div>
            {{/each}}
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ac-wizard-step" data-wizard-step="3">
        <div class="ac-step-heading"><span>STEP 04</span><h2>Select the Starting Sleeve</h2><p>The sleeve is the current body. It supplies Strength, Perception, Health and body-specific technology limits; the DHF identity remains separate.</p></div>
        <div class="ac-wizard-grid">
          <article class="ac-panel">
            <label class="ac-select-field"><span>Sleeve Type</span><select name="sleeveType" data-live-summary>{{#each sleeveTypes}}<option value="{{id}}">{{label}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
            <div class="ac-callout"><strong>AI characters:</strong> the guided creator requires a synthetic sleeve because the 2020 Core does not give a simple age-table chassis for AI. Building/mainframe AIs can still be created manually.</div>
          </article>
          <aside class="ac-explainer">
            {{#each sleeveTypes}}
            <div data-sleeve-panel="{{id}}" {{#unless @first}}hidden{{/unless}}><i class="fa-solid fa-dna"></i><h3>{{label}}</h3><p>{{description}}</p><div class="ac-tech-spec"><span>STR {{lookup limits.strength 0}}–{{lookup limits.strength 1}}</span><span>PER {{lookup limits.perception 0}}–{{lookup limits.perception 1}}</span><span>TECH {{limits.techCapacity}}</span></div></div>
            {{/each}}
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ac-wizard-step" data-wizard-step="4">
        <div class="ac-step-heading"><span>STEP 05</span><h2>Set Attributes</h2><p>All six Attributes are visible here at once. The two cyan-coded values are sleeve hardware; the four violet-coded values belong to the persistent DHF.</p></div>
        <article class="ac-panel">
          <div class="ac-creator-attributes">
            {{#each attributeHelp}}
            <label class="ac-creator-attribute {{class}}"><span class="code">{{code}}</span><span class="copy"><strong>{{name}}</strong><small>{{description}}</small></span><input type="number" name="{{id}}" value="30" data-live-summary></label>
            {{/each}}
          </div>
          <div class="ac-callout">Standard Stack Attributes begin at 30. Higher values are available here for pre-generated or GM-authored final characters; normal play advancement uses Stack Points and the system's advancement procedures.</div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="ac-wizard-step" data-wizard-step="5">
        <div class="ac-step-heading"><span>STEP 06</span><h2>Resources & Economy</h2><p>The wizard calculates most starting resources automatically from age, Attributes, Archetype and Variant. Only values the rules leave open are requested from you.</p></div>
        <div class="ac-wizard-grid">
          <article class="ac-panel">
            <label class="ac-select-field"><span>Wealth Override <small>Leave blank to use the Archetype baseline.</small></span><input type="number" name="wealth" value="" min="0" max="6" data-live-summary placeholder="Archetype default"></label>
            <div data-ai-only hidden>
              <label class="ac-select-field"><span>AI Stack Points <small>Required because the Core gives AI no age-based starting SP row.</small></span><input type="number" name="manualSP" value="" min="0"></label>
              <label class="ac-select-field"><span>AI Influence Points <small>Required for the same reason; the wizard will not invent a value.</small></span><input type="number" name="manualIP" value="" min="0"></label>
            </div>
          </article>
          <aside class="ac-explainer">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-coins"></i><h3>What the system creates</h3>
            <ul><li><strong>Health:</strong> rolled from sleeve type and Strength Bonus.</li><li><strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> derived from Strength.</li><li><strong>Ego / SP / IP:</strong> calculated from the source procedures and variant modifiers where deterministic.</li><li><strong>Skills:</strong> all 32 are embedded at the Archetype starting levels.</li><li><strong>Baggage:</strong> age-based rolls are resolved automatically.</li><li><strong>Starting Package:</strong> package Traits and gear note are embedded.</li></ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ac-wizard-step" data-wizard-step="6">
        <div class="ac-step-heading"><span>STEP 07</span><h2>Review & Instantiate</h2><p>Confirm the concept. The creator will make the Actor, starting sleeve, full Skill list, package content and deterministic starting resources in one operation.</p></div>
        <article class="ac-panel ac-review-panel">
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>True DHF</span><strong data-summary="name">New DHF</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>Public Name</span><strong data-summary="publicName">New DHF</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>Age</span><strong data-summary="age">30 years</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>Archetype</span><strong data-summary="archetype">Civilian</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>Starting Package</span><strong data-summary="package">Custom / choose later</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>Variant</span><strong data-summary="variant">Standard DHF</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>Sleeve</span><strong data-summary="sleeve">birth</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row wide"><span>Attributes</span><strong data-summary="attributes">STR 30 · PER 30 · EMP 30 · WIL 30 · ACU 30 · INT 30</strong></div>
          <div class="ac-review-row"><span>Wealth</span><strong data-summary="wealth">Archetype default</strong></div>
        </article>
        <div class="ac-callout success"><strong>Ready.</strong> Anything not chosen by the source rules remains editable on the finished sheet rather than being silently invented.</div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <footer class="ac-wizard-footer">
    <button type="button" data-action="prevStep" disabled><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back</button>
    <div><span>2020 Core rules chassis</span><small>Guided workflow · editable after creation</small></div>
    <button type="button" data-action="nextStep" class="ac-primary-action">Continue <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i></button>
    <button type="button" data-action="create" class="ac-primary-action" hidden><i class="fa-solid fa-user-plus"></i> Create DHF</button>
  </footer>
</section>
